            <ArticleTitle>Antiinflammatory and analgesic effects of Carthamus lanatus aerial parts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>559-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fractions of methanol, dichloromethane, water extracts and volatiles of Carthamus lanatus aerial parts given by oral route at a dose of 2 mg/kg showed significant antiinflammatory activities in rats. On the contrary, only the water fraction of MeOH extract possesses a significant analgesic activity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
